EXAMPLES
    Look around from home:
        pwd
        ls
        tree

    Read a pin and react to it in a script:
        in 14
        if $IN14==1 then
            echo pressed
        fi

    Write a small file without opening the editor:
        echo hello there > greeting.txt
        cat greeting.txt

    Log the temperature every 10 minutes, then look at it
    (/etc/crontab line, then at the prompt):
        every 10m temp | log -n /root/temp.csv
        plot -f 2 /root/temp.csv

    Wait for a button on GPIO14 (to GND) in a script:
        in -w 14 up fall && echo pressed

    Find Python files and count them:
        ls /bin | grep .py | wc

    A loop in a script (count.sh):
        for i 1 5
            if $i == 3 then
                continue
            fi
            echo round $i
        done

    Save a listing, then look at it:
        ls -l /bin > /root/bin.txt
        head -n 5 /root/bin.txt

    Set the clock from the internet (W boards):
        wifi myssid mypassword
        date ntp

    Watch an input every second (Ctrl-C stops):
        watch 1 in 14

    Set a custom prompt for this session:
        export PS1=\w>
        unset PS1

    Join a network, then serve a control page for the onboard LED
    and two extra pins, with a live input and an analog reading:
        wifi myssid mypassword
        httpd -p secret LED 16 IN14 ADC0
        httpd stop

